  "configuration_id": "config_012",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-3 results (config_029: 0.7207, config_042: 0.7150, config_001: 0.7062) all share scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile, and consistently show concat > weighted fusion and transformer ≥ avgpool aggregation. config_012 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is the only untested variant in this best-performing 2×2 aggregation×fusion grid. Question: Does transformer aggregation provide a benefit even with weighted fusion, or is the concat+transformer synergy specific to concat? While the evidence strongly favors concat (0.715 vs 0.706 at avgpool), testing this final cell completes the design-space picture and is the only remaining configuration that could theoretically exceed our current best of 0.7207. As the final experiment, this is the highest-expected-value exploitation choice. Expected cost: ~4.5–5 GPU hours (comparable to config_029 at 4.65 h and config_042 at 4.49 h, since it uses the same imagenet_vit_l encoder and transformer aggregation). Total budget would be ~56.5–57 GPU hours."
}

